{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons","id":449519,"title":"Fictional Pantheons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-19T11:43:21-07:00","id":449519,"title":"Fictional Pantheons?","content":"Simply put, fictional pantheons are literary creations. William Blake created a profound mythology, Tolkien created an appealing one, neither counts as a real world pantheon people worshiped. However, both men's writtings give enough details that you could create PSPs and reasonable descriptions for their pantheons. In the 1ed of Scion, the Atlantean, Yankee, and Allied, pantheons were fictional pantheons in this sense.<br /> <br /> The question is, do Fictional Pantheons have a place in Scion?<br /> <br /> If fictional pantheons have a place in Scion, what is that place? Might their be a campaign, given as a worked example, set in a Space Opera setting with competing pantheons promoting different value systems for humanity? Or perhaps a group of fictional gods, like Urizen and his tribe, stated out as a demostraition of how myths are turned into workable pantheons for games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:12:37-07:00","id":449651,"title":"","content":"Um...I'm pretty sure that &quot;superheroes&quot; will be addressed in Scion 2E. Although I'd think it's going to be more like &quot;superhero-ification&quot; of deities. (The best example is Thor.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:39:57-07:00","id":449727,"title":"","content":"This tends to be a fairly contentious issue.<br /> <br /> Significant portions of the fan base prefer Scion to be focused on real-world mythology; with fictional Pantheons only arising out of PC actions (aka PCs starting their own as they become deities), while others prefer having the mix 1e started by adding the mentioned fictional ones.<br /> <br /> I personally feel that Scion does have a place for fictional Pantheons. Though it should be a secondary expansion while the core material focuses on real mythologies. The only exception to this for me should be when the core books discuss creating Pantheons (since again, PCs making their own should be part of the game) as fictional ones serve a useful purpose as examples for how to craft ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:01:50-07:00","id":449748,"title":"","content":"I think the fun of Scion is that you're playing with numerous ancient myths in a new setting, and putting figures from all over the world into a setting with one another. Making a pantheon up from whole cloth defeats that purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T16:58:49-07:00","id":449900,"title":"","content":"Operating on the premise that if it\u2019s not Factual, it must therefore be Fictional, there is a class of Fictional Pantheons that I believe <i>very definitely</i> have a place in <b>Scion</b>: namely, Pantheons that are built around real-world mythologies that are so factually sparse that most of the Pantheon has to be invented by the writers. Examples of such are the Arabian and Gaulish Pantheons. <br /> <br /> The above illustrates a further complication: there really isn\u2019t a hard line separating \u201cFact-based\u201d Pantheons from Fictional ones; it\u2019s a continuum, and the question isn\u2019t really \u201cdo fictional Pantheons have a place?\u201d so much as \u201cwhere do you draw the line?\u201d Implicit in my opening statement is the notion that if the writer has to make up most of the details himself, the Pantheon is fictional; but I could just as easily see an argument that if the Pantheon has or had a thriving base of worshippers, it should be considered \u201cfactual\u201d, even if 90% of the game material pertaining to it is made up. <br /> <br /> The Atlantean Pantheon demonstrates another \u201cshade of gray\u201d, where the fiction\u2019s premise is that the Pantheon <i>did</i> have worshippers at one point; but that the worshippers have been gone for so long that their very existence is now in doubt. My own inclination would be to draw the line between the Gaulish and Arabian Pantheons on the one hand, and the Atlantean Pantheon on the other; but really, the two examples aren\u2019t <i>that</i> far apart. <br /> <br /> Then you get into what I\u2019d call the Fabulous Pantheons (as in \u201cFables\u201d) \u2014 Pantheons that are built on personas that nobody has ever <i>seriously</i> believed in or worshipped, but which are firmly rooted in the public imagination nonetheless. The National Pantheons fit this group, as do figures such as Santa Claus and the Tooth Fairy. My inclination would be to avoid building Pantheons around such things, unless you\u2019re dealing with a Shard setting that is specifically geared toward them. <br /> <br /> Tolkein\u2019s mythology is an interesting case: at first blush, it looks like it was something that Tolkein made up out of whole cloth, and thus should be considered about as far to the opposite side of the spectrum from, say, the Greek Pantheon. But if you look at it more closely, it\u2019s not that clear-cut: Tolkein\u2019s \u201cgods\u201d are closely patterned after a real-world religion that has an enormous following even today: that is, they\u2019re a reconceptualization of Abrahamic mythology. This would arguably place Tolkein\u2019s Pantheon in a slightly less fictional \u201cshade of gray\u201d than a Pantheon featuring Columbia or Santa Claus. Still firmly in the realm of fiction for Scion\u2019s purposes, mind you. <br /> <br /> All that said: the bottom line for me is that there are <i>so</i> many unexplored possibilities in the hundreds of Pantheons that everyone here would agree are Scion-appropriate, and so much diverse possibilities among them, that I see little point in the developers pursuing any that are primarily made up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:19:27-07:00","id":449970,"title":"","content":"Tolkien's pantheon is also a re-imagining of Finnish mythology as well. And you can definitely see Old English all over everything he did. So it's definitely fantasy by way of scholarship. For the purposes of story-telling. As opposed to Blake, who looks like he was trying to shoehorn some Zoroastrian/Gnosticism into a set of tales designed to illustrate a political objective. (He's in good company. That's pretty much what Plato did for Atlantis... err... not the Scion Atlantis, the one the Atlantic Ocean was named after.) <br /> <br /> There are a lot of &quot;fantastic&quot; mythologies out there that are largely made up but are based in and around some version of a quasi-historic version of the world in which we live. I think you could probably integrate those into a Scion setting pretty well, if you wanted to do so. You would be stretching the &quot;game of modern mythology&quot; to &quot;game of fantastic mythology with a modern setting&quot;, but that's a huge jump. <br /> <br /> So, though, I don't see myself doing it for one of my own games (I LOVE me my bookcase of myth books), I definitely can see creating a &quot;lost pantheon of a vanished people&quot; much like the Atlantean pantheon, if that served a purpose for the stories I was trying to tell. It's based on the modern concepts of &quot;Lost Atlantis&quot; so you have source material to work from. On the same level, I'm guessing you could use the relevant new age-type sources to create pantheons for Lemuria or Mu or Z. You could go another way and base an Atlantean pantheon off of, say, the Gods of Atlantis from DC comics (Aquaman &amp; Arion) and work it up that way. Similarly, in a different vein, Lovecraft's Great Old One integrate into this world fairly seemlessly. They could definitely be lurking around behind the scenes in a world of fantastic mythology. Perhaps as Titans? Unless you want to go there with playing the Son of Hastur, the Daughter of Ithaqua and the.... Spawn? of Cthulhu. With an interesting level of Squick-factor. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you are going to keep the modern setting, I think you might have a harder time integrating something like Tolkien's mythology. You could do so, but I think it's going to be enough work that you probably should have a really good reason for doing it. It seems to me that it would only be marginally less difficult to integrate the Valar into the modern world (and have them getting busy with the Second Children of Iluvatar) than it would be to create a version of Middle Earth re-tooled for Scion. Blakes would be a much better fit with a modern world, or at least one from a century or so ago. As it should be, since that's what he's talking about. It's a lot like having a fantastic (phatasmagorical?) version of the various Angelic pantheons that are out there. <br /> <br /> As for &quot;nigh fictional&quot; pantheons. I think they need to be CLEARLY marked as such. People learn a lot from gaming, by osmosis at the very least. Thinking that the Gaulish pantheon as presented represents the Gaulish pantheon that we-know-don't-know-much-about is a disservice to what we DO know about Gaulish myths and legends. There is a big difference between knitting together an interpretation of myths from what we know and what will work for the purposes of the game and taking a few factoids and making the rest of the story whole-cloth. That being said, I think the Gaulish pantheon is relatively cool. It seems a little more different from Irish myths than it could have been and that distance was made up wit hpure make-believe, but, sure, why not? If you want to explore &quot;this is the pantheon that Fate hates&quot; it's right there for you and it does get some verisimilitude for the use of what info there is. <br /> <br /> I think John &amp; Anne's Arabian pantheon is a little more portable. As she said when discussing it, there is definitely some info out there, but some of it is just GONE. Actively suprressed out of existence. Not recorded in any meaningfull way. And some of those are parts a pantheon needs for a Scion write up, so what are you going to do? Anne did a great job taking what there was and trying to figure out something cool to use to fill in. Some of it from out of her head. Some of it based loosely on various customs and folkways of the relevant culture. I think her Arabian works a bit better for me for those reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T21:48:38-07:00","id":450127,"title":"","content":"On the Tolkein Mythology thing, I could actually see something <i>like</i> that showing up at some point, as the ultimate \u201cforgotten gods of a forgotten people\u201d sort of thing. Not so much Tolkein\u2019s <i>specific</i> mythology, mind you; but maybe an adaptation of the Exalted Incarna as a Pantheon. Or not. \ud83d\ude1b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T05:55:43-07:00","id":450344,"title":"","content":"*shrugs*<br /> I'm in the process of creating my own pantheons, myths, cosmology, etc...<br /> And it's very different from what has already been made. (Old myths don't really go over well today)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T08:53:31-07:00","id":450491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=450344#post450344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs*<br /> I'm in the process of creating my own pantheons, myths, cosmology, etc...<br /> And it's very different from what has already been made. (Old myths don't really go over well today)</div> </div> </div> </div>On what do you base that observation?<br /> <br /> They seem to be doing fabulously at the box office, either directly or indirectly in some of re-tooled form. Same with books, in the fantasy genre, science fiction, and &quot;literature&quot; (whatever that means). Comic books too. Not just the popular ones but the ones that get acclaim. And so on and so on. Those myths show up in pretty much every field of creative endeavor and even, quite often, in other fields as well. <br /> <br /> In fact, considering how they are told, re-told and re-retold, there aren't really many stories that aren't, in their essence &quot;old myths&quot;. By modern theories of literature analysis and symbolic anthropology, there aren't that many different basic stories that have every been told. And the original telling of those stories were myths, legends and folklore. Myths are embedded at the fundamental levels of culture. So, in point of fact, since you are an example of 5,000, 10,0000, 20,000 or 150,000 years of human culture (depending on how you slice &quot;human&quot; and &quot;culture&quot;), anything you make will be informed by old myths and will most likely be the x-thousandth iteration of the same basic concepts. <br /> <br /> It seems like, considering that this is a forum devoted to game that is fundamentally about &quot;old myths&quot;, while taking said game out of the box and re-arranging it to suit your own needs is absolutely cool, disparaging the core concepts is an attempt to be deliberately provocative, particularly in the dismissive fashion you addressed your comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:04:18-07:00","id":450673,"title":"","content":"Human sacrifice and stuff is frowned on today...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:35:55-07:00","id":450704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=450127#post450127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Tolkein Mythology thing, I could actually see something <i>like</i> that showing up at some point, as the ultimate \u201cforgotten gods of a forgotten people\u201d sort of thing. Not so much Tolkein\u2019s <i>specific</i> mythology, mind you; but maybe an adaptation of the Exalted Incarna as a Pantheon. Or not. \ud83d\ude1b</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe some young, particularly nerdy Scions decide to model themselves after the Valar and end up being Fatebound into actually being them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:41:10-07:00","id":450712,"title":"","content":"It may, indeed, be frowned upon. However, it was very much a part of those cultures that participated in it. If you wish to not include it, then you can simply not include that Pantheon into your game. That is the beauty of rpg's: You can include whatever you want and disregard whatever you want. However, you should also go ahead and talk it over with your players to not include the Pantheon. Some of them may resonate strongly with the Atzlanti. <br /> However, it is commendable that you wish to create your own Pantheons. I have toyed around with the idea myself. Creating one in the vein of Rise of the Guardians (I can hear people groaning from here) simply because these myths fit for those who do not wish to deal with specific cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:59:40-07:00","id":450773,"title":"","content":"&quot;<b>Was</b> is the operative word. Human sacrifice does not go over well <b>today</b>. I think it's kinda strange that people want things as &quot;real&quot; as it can be, but ignore the fact that by today's standards, sacrificing newborns (looking at you Moloch) puts a deity firmly on the other side. For the most part, were I to put together a bunch of deities from other mythologies, I would have back stories that tell how they acclimated to various time-frames. I would cobble together another group of deities that refused to recognized the winds of change and prefer to try to relive their glory gory days. And they would be the villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:33:59-07:00","id":450796,"title":"","content":"Human sacrifice is alive and well. We call it &quot;Capital Punishment&quot; here in the USA. Voluntary euthanasia. Double blind drug trials including a placebo for people with lethal medical conditions. We justify those the exact same way that other cultures justified their version of human sacrifice. It preserves the social order. It promotes the public good. <br /> <br /> In fact the difference between a modern war, of aggression where you &quot;kill them where you find them&quot; and an Aztec War of Flowers with its &quot;find them, capture them, then kill them&quot; is really a matter of location of the homicide rather the function served. <br /> <br /> We definitely still have sacrifice of newborns that is functionally not much different than the kind of infant exposure from Ancient Greece, some West African tribes, etc. but, the situations and issues involved are beyond the scope of discussion I find myself comfortable discussing in an open forum.<br /> <br /> The thing about people is that they pretty much seem to be people no matter when and where you find them. They will definitely find different ways to do things, but it will be different ways to do the same things. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:42:53-07:00","id":450802,"title":"","content":"You can play games with the English language to pretty it up as much as you want, killing babies in such a manner isn't acceptable today. (I'm reminded of a time when I had to go to court and was watching an earlier court case. It was amazing how easily the judge sliced through all the bs that a lawyer was trying to sell.) It is what it is. Murder isn't acceptable today. If you believe differently, then you should not be playing games. You should instead be seeing a psychiatrist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:01:31-07:00","id":450844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=450704#post450704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some young, particularly nerdy Scions decide to model themselves after the Valar and end up being Fatebound into actually being them?</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL. I am so glad that I didn't get a Visitation at certain points of my life. It would such to have to be Orome or Mandos for all eternity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:59:26-07:00","id":452966,"title":"","content":"Only when people can see you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T15:36:28-07:00","id":453278,"title":"","content":"Only when people who have read the Silmarillion can see me.<br /> <br /> Then I will lay unto them their ultimate DOOM.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T21:14:28-07:00","id":453769,"title":"","content":"I don't see a major problem with them being included. The gods and scions draw strength from legends and stories told about them, so I imagine that if a fictional pantheon became popular enough, mortals could inadvertently bring them to life without realizing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T23:46:54-07:00","id":453916,"title":"","content":"At least as far as we know, belief does <i>not</i> fuel or create Gods in Scion or Scion2E. So, no, no matter how many people believe Superman will save them (is that.. like four people? Who honestly believes that Superman or Elrond exists, in <i>any</i> form?) he will not manifest as a God. Nor will The Almighty Dollar, or Lady Liberty, or Hawkgirl.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do think &quot;Lost&quot; Pantheons could work. I'd be fine with, say, a game about the Gods of Humanity fighting against invaders from The Great Dark Beyond, or even from a pre-human history. Dinosaur Gods! Neanderthal Gods! The possibilities are practically endless!<br /> <br /> Just not Superman-endless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 03-23-2015, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T05:44:40-07:00","id":454133,"title":"","content":"Being the Scion of a dinosaur god would be really fricken metal!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T05:41:34-07:00","id":491550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=450127#post450127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Tolkein Mythology thing, I could actually see something <i>like</i> that showing up at some point, as the ultimate \u201cforgotten gods of a forgotten people\u201d sort of thing. Not so much Tolkein\u2019s <i>specific</i> mythology, mind you; but maybe an adaptation of the Exalted Incarna as a Pantheon. Or not. \ud83d\ude1b</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, not in Scion, but in a Champions game, i once played a PC descended from a proto-finnish/baltic fire spirit that supposedly inspired Tolkien's idea of the Balrog. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So certain things are certainly doable depending on your references and how you adapt them.<br /> <br /> I agree that pantheons springing wholy from literature doesn't fit well with what the books tells us about the gods origins and how fatebinding works. That said human imagination can resonate with and shape them, what along with the fact titans and their avatar have no clearly defined numbers, open some curious wiggle room.<br /> <br /> It won't make things happen on itself, but as some titanspawn or avatars interact with mortals and a few survive to tell tales that later ressonate with them....who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-25-2015, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T23:26:56-07:00","id":585707,"title":"","content":"This gets me thinking about Jack Kirby's New Gods. Would that be one Pantheon, divided in it's ideology, or two opposing Pantheons? Or would the gods of New Genesis be one Pantheon, and those of Apocolips (That spelling is intentional, for those who don't know) be their Titan enemy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T05:57:48-07:00","id":585944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=585707#post585707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gets me thinking about Jack Kirby's New Gods. Would that be one Pantheon, divided in it's ideology, or two opposing Pantheons? Or would the gods of New Genesis be one Pantheon, and those of Apocolips (That spelling is intentional, for those who don't know) be their Titan enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty good question that - i'm somewhat tempted to see them as one combined pantheon, with the world of Apokolips under Darkseid being the most titan-touched part of the whole.<br /> Or at least the most Titan-seeming - order is a big deal of Darkseid's style unlike one's run-of-the-mill titanspawn and particularly in Kirby's take of the Fourth World there's much to show New Genesis ain't quite as good as one mistakenly think due to all the shiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:03:14-07:00","id":586194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=585707#post585707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gets me thinking about Jack Kirby's New Gods. Would that be one Pantheon, divided in it's ideology, or two opposing Pantheons? Or would the gods of New Genesis be one Pantheon, and those of Apocolips (That spelling is intentional, for those who don't know) be their Titan enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also an issue with ancient mythological pantheons as well. The Persian, mostly pre-Zoorastrian pantheon, the Yazatas is effectively the Asuras or &quot;somewhat bad, sometime enemies&quot; opposition gods of the Devas of Hindu mythology. Likewise, to the Yazatas are effectively their opposition, the deevils. Plus here are insane amounts of cross-over between the two with gods that are almost completely the same between the two. The Yazata book discussed the situation lightly, but defaulted to the Scion &quot;standard&quot; of Pantheon vs. Titan default instead of Pantheon vs. Pantheon.<br /> <br /> It also happens within a culture. The Sumerian gods are divided into two groups the Annuna (Annunaki) and the Igigi who are partially, kinda, a little opposed. Or the Norse, where the Vanir and Aesir are buddy-buddy now, but they used to be not very friendly at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T22:55:38-07:00","id":586827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=585707#post585707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gets me thinking about Jack Kirby's New Gods. Would that be one Pantheon, divided in it's ideology, or two opposing Pantheons? Or would the gods of New Genesis be one Pantheon, and those of Apocolips (That spelling is intentional, for those who don't know) be their Titan enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd say they qualify as the same pantheon for a number of reasons. Their planets were originally one much larger world, they have similar technology to each other, and they were both formed in the aftermath of a war between the elder gods. Too many similarities to say they're different groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, I just found out that Hathor is apparently the most powerful goddess to have ever existed in mythology. Does this still hold up in Scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-11-2015, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T07:39:32-07:00","id":587112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=586827#post586827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way, I just found out that Hathor is apparently the most powerful goddess to have ever existed in mythology. Does this still hold up in Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea where you got that from, but Hathor isn't even mentioned in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T09:07:35-07:00","id":587180,"title":"","content":"I'm not <i>opposed</i> to doing the Gods of Peg\u0101na or other fictional pantheons (maybe even a return of the much-maligned Atlantean pantheon as a dead offshoot or rivals of the Theoi) as stretch goals or one-off products, but they won't be in any of the corebooks. Even then, it'd be down the line - plenty of &quot;real&quot; pantheons exist that deserve the spotlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:38:02-07:00","id":587280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=587180#post587180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not <i>opposed</i> to doing the Gods of Peg\u0101na or other fictional pantheons (maybe even a return of the much-maligned Atlantean pantheon as a dead offshoot or rivals of the Theoi) as stretch goals or one-off products, but they won't be in any of the corebooks. Even then, it'd be down the line - plenty of &quot;real&quot; pantheons exist that deserve the spotlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telchines\" target=\"_blank\">Telchines</a> are the actual ancient allies that became foes of the Theoi. But the Atlanteans would make a good worked example pantheon. Another worked example pantheon idea might take a world like Flash Gordon's Mongo, give that world a dominant pantheon, and work that out as a fictional example.<br /> <br /> Rereading the description, I wonder if Scion's Atlanteans aren't based on the Telchines after all. They are similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:22:57-07:00","id":589407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=586194#post586194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also an issue with ancient mythological pantheons as well. The Persian, mostly pre-Zoorastrian pantheon, the Yazatas is effectively the Asuras or &quot;somewhat bad, sometime enemies&quot; opposition gods of the Devas of Hindu mythology. Likewise, to the Yazatas are effectively their opposition, the deevils. Plus here are insane amounts of cross-over between the two with gods that are almost completely the same between the two. The Yazata book discussed the situation lightly, but defaulted to the Scion &quot;standard&quot; of Pantheon vs. Titan default instead of Pantheon vs. Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually more like the <b>words</b> each people used for &quot;local/rival deity&quot; - Deva/Asura in the Indian subcontinent, Ahura/Daeva in the Persian area of influence - were opposites rather than the deities. Mitra appears in both as a deity and &quot;Verethragna&quot; is basically a title of Indra, Vrithragna, the slayer of Vrithra, among other tidbits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=587280#post587280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telchines\" target=\"_blank\">Telchines</a> are the actual ancient allies that became foes of the Theoi. But the Atlanteans would make a good worked example pantheon. Another worked example pantheon idea might take a world like Flash Gordon's Mongo, give that world a dominant pantheon, and work that out as a fictional example.<br /> <br /> Rereading the description, I wonder if Scion's Atlanteans aren't based on the Telchines after all. They are similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect they are and i think the connection has been mentioned somewhere, though if it was in the books or some writer in the forums, right now i have no idea at all<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T11:01:54-08:00","id":770841,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else have an idea on a fictional pantheons in Scion?<br /> <br /> By the way, could an older pantheon choose to disguise itself as a fictional pantheon to gain followers in the modern world? Say that a group of leftover deities from Lost pantheons bands together and decides to gain followers in modern Europe and California by Hi-Jacking the reputations of fictional characters as a means of promoting their values and ideals.<br /> <br /> We are told that the Gods promote certain virtues, that pantheons define themselves through their values and virtues, the arts and legend are powerful means of promoting ideals. So why wouldn't real gods swipe the reputations of Fictional deities to promote values important to them? Heck, why wouldn't Zeus disguise himself as Superman if it furthered his goals and ideals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T20:08:36-08:00","id":772752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons#post449519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, fictional pantheons are literary creations. William Blake created a profound mythology, Tolkien created an appealing one, neither counts as a real world pantheon people worshiped. However, both men's writtings give enough details that you could create PSPs and reasonable descriptions for their pantheons. In the 1ed of Scion, the Atlantean, Yankee, and Allied, pantheons were fictional pantheons in this sense.<br /> <br /> The question is, do Fictional Pantheons have a place in Scion?<br /> <br /> If fictional pantheons have a place in Scion, what is that place? Might their be a campaign, given as a worked example, set in a Space Opera setting with competing pantheons promoting different value systems for humanity? Or perhaps a group of fictional gods, like Urizen and his tribe, stated out as a demostraition of how myths are turned into workable pantheons for games?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's kind of difficult to discern what might count as a fictional pantheon or not. Just look at the Aesir. They believe there are 9 different worlds out there full of giants and elves and pixies and dwarves and so on. Sounds pretty similar to works like Tolkien and yet people believed in them at the time. The gods are made and influenced by Legend. The head cannon I go by is that if enough people believe in it, they can create a pantheon based on their unified beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:00:51-08:00","id":773070,"title":"","content":"Fiction in itself does shape gods in the Scion setting, thought its popularity may influence beings identified with it by way of fatebinding.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that appently a number of gods started as titans, or at least titan avatars, themselves and slowly shaped themselves in gods by some form of symbiosis with the wellspring of ideas and imagery that is the human collective imagination/unconscious that shapes fate. So, theoretically, it could happen again that some new set of values and imagery gaining steam with a large number of people might attract some obscure titanic aspect/avatar or other and shape it into some modern form of deity, though fiction that borders into phylosophy, like maybe Objectivism for a reasonably fresh example, might work better for this than Harry Potter and escapist entertainment.<br /> <br /> Or not - Harry Potter is full of fairy tales tropes and imagery, so who's to say a bunch of lesser immortals might not be inadvertently affected in some way or another by the series success? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T15:39:08-08:00","id":1022485,"title":"","content":"Art has powerful effects on humanity's worldview. Could pantheons use art to cut the bonds of fate and/or shape Humanity's values?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T09:35:18-08:00","id":1022803,"title":"","content":"Humanity (Modern humans) has been around for nearly 200,000 years, but we know very little about that history. Most of what we know comes from the last 5000 years, and there is virtually nothing known beyond 10,000 years ago. 95% of human history is more or less lost or forgotten. How many tribes and civilizations might have arisen and fallen within that time? Are we to assume that our earliest ancestors didn't worship gods of any form? How many lost pantheons could there be... Gods that were once worshiped by hundreds, thousands or even millions of people (okay... maybe not millions, but still)?<br /> <br /> This is where I believe that many of the &quot;fictional&quot; pantheons could come into their own.<br /> <br /> \u200bMany have argued when the Atlantean Pantheon came out that they (the Atlanteans) should have worshiped the Greek Pantheon because the one confirmed source of information on their society said they did (despite the fact that he was likely looking at them through his own bias and equating their gods to the ones he knew of). I found such a position to be... unrealistic given the fact that Atlantis vanished thousands of years earlier... before even the rise of the Egyptians (often credited as the oldest known Pantheon)... when the would be Greek Gods were not really much of a unified pantheon (at least their mythology was still forming with the Greek tribes). This is why I found the Atlantean Pantheon to be one of the most intriguing Pantheons in Scion 1E... a lost pantheon from a civilization shrouded in myth and legend... and not just new names for old gods (something that has already been done to death with the Greek/Roman pantheon).<br /> <br /> \u200bHow many other mythical civilizations are there that have vanished in the mists of history? Lemuria... Mu... Thule... Ys... Shambhala... and many others that have been lost to history. Are we to assume that the people of these lands merely worshiped the same gods as later civilizations... just with different names? With a new age of Legends beginning, it could be the only time such forgotten and lost pantheons to resurface and reclaim their place as powerful Pantheons... and for their civilizations to be remembered as something more than mere myth.<br /> <br /> \u200bYes, these pantheons will technically be fictional... in that there is no real knowledge of their existence (and are likely created from whole cloth), but they can fill the gap needed to make these mythical places part of the World's history (at least in this setting). Sure, you can have Atlanteans worship Greek Gods, the People of Ys worshiping the Celtic Pantheon or Lemuria worshiping a number of other pantheons... but that would likely make these places seem less... mythic. Now having a Scion of the fallen and traitorous Atlantean Gods (one interpretation of their fall mind you) who is trying to redeem his once noble heritage... seems a lot more interesting and mythic than having him be just another Scion of Poseidon... doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T20:06:20-08:00","id":1025249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons#post449519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, do Fictional Pantheons have a place in Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, now we have a whole stretch goal on how to build your own pantheon, including fictional ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:05:14-08:00","id":1181768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=453916#post453916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least as far as we know, belief does <i>not</i> fuel or create Gods in Scion or Scion2E. So, no, no matter how many people believe Superman will save them (is that.. like four people? Who honestly believes that Superman or Elrond exists, in <i>any</i> form?) he will not manifest as a God. Nor will The Almighty Dollar, or Lady Liberty, or Hawkgirl.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do think &amp;quot;Lost&amp;quot; Pantheons could work. I'd be fine with, say, a game about the Gods of Humanity fighting against invaders from The Great Dark Beyond, or even from a pre-human history. Dinosaur Gods! Neanderthal Gods! The possibilities are practically endless!<br /> <br /> Just not Superman-endless.</div> </div> </div> </div>If lost gods would work, what about gods that worked behind the scenes? Might gods that stayed out of the limelight to accomplish worthy goals still have legend and scions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:10:29-08:00","id":1181771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=585707#post585707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gets me thinking about Jack Kirby's New Gods. Would that be one Pantheon, divided in it's ideology, or two opposing Pantheons? Or would the gods of New Genesis be one Pantheon, and those of Apocolips (That spelling is intentional, for those who don't know) be their Titan enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of Darkseid he doesn't need to be a titan to end worlds. I'd give the two groups of deities the same PSP with certain levels being mirror images of each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T11:19:15-08:00","id":1182325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=585707#post585707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gets me thinking about Jack Kirby's New Gods. Would that be one Pantheon, divided in it's ideology, or two opposing Pantheons? Or would the gods of New Genesis be one Pantheon, and those of Apocolips (That spelling is intentional, for those who don't know) be their Titan enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, just recently found out about these guys...<br /> <br /> If you want to incorporate Titans into the DC mythos, you might wanna take a look at some people called <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5ATxT1MUZE8\" target=\"_blank\">The Endless.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-04-2018, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T14:14:49-08:00","id":1182380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=1181771#post1181771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the case of Darkseid he doesn't need to be a titan to end worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly thinking about them having Titan/Dark Virtues. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/449519-fictional-pantheons?p=1182325#post1182325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, just recently found out about these guys...<br /> <br /> If you want to incorporate Titans into the DC mythos, you might wanna take a look at some people called <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5ATxT1MUZE8&quot;]The</a> Endless.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the Endless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 02-04-2018, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}